  "body": "Implements issue #7360 (task 13046, lane code-x): the server-side identity backup from the #5033 design decision, as a new `pkgs/id/src/backup.rs` module.\n\n## What lands\n- **Record** keyed by `H(pub) = SHA-256(identity public key)` holding exactly the #5033 item-2 field set (envelope bytes, envelope SHA-256, blob size, upload/download timestamps, monotone upload epoch, throttle counters, `restore_epoch`, deletion tombstone). `BackupRecord::stored_field_names()` is pinned by a test to the decision's list, so a new stored field fails CI until the decision is amended.\n- **Upload**: envelope bytes + `Sign_identity(H(pub) || envelope_sha256 || epoch_be)`; signature verified against the named public key, non-increasing epochs rejected, only a valid higher-epoch upload overwrites. The blob is the `key_envelope` v1 envelope byte-for-byte (108 bytes, validated shape on upload); the server never sees a passphrase.\n- **Download**: per-identity budget of 10/hour and 50/day counted with weighted fixed windows in the `abuse.rs` limiter shape; refusals carry retry-after. Per-IP/global limits stay with the endpoint layer's `AbuseEvaluator`.\n- **Delete**: signed at the record's current epoch; ciphertext + counters dropped, only the tombstone (`H(pub)` + final epoch) remains; replaying the pre-delete signed upload cannot resurrect it. Account deletion purges the tombstone.\n- **Restore**: client restore recovers the key from passphrase + downloaded envelope using only the existing `key_envelope::decrypt` path (wrong passphrase fails locally, no server signal). Download-for-restore increments `restore_epoch` and notifies bound devices; the restored key is not authoritative for new group epochs until notifications are confirmed. **No rotation flag** is introduced (#2380 owns that representation).\n- **Client create**: reuses `key_envelope::encrypt` exactly, with a weak-passphrase warning at creation per item 3's guessing-cost analysis.\n\n## Tests (each names its oracle — the #5033 decision items)\n- Stored field set equals the item-2 list; no rotation field.\n- Bad signature / equal / stale epoch rejected; higher-epoch signed upload replaces the blob.\n- Malformed envelopes (length, magic, version) refused with the named error.\n- The 11th download in an hour and the 51st in a day are refused with retry-after; a proptest checks the budget invariant (admitted per fixed window ≤ limit) over arbitrary monotone interleavings.\n- Restore round-trip recovers the key; wrong passphrase fails locally.\n- Restore increments `restore_epoch`, notifies bound devices, blocks authoritativeness until confirmation.\n- Signed delete removes ciphertext; the pre-delete signed upload replay does not resurrect; tombstone purge works.\n\nScope note: this is the backup record/endpoint logic at the `pkgs/id` library layer (store, signature/epoch/budget enforcement, client create/restore helpers). HTTP wiring into a running server endpoint composes these functions with the existing `abuse::AbuseEvaluator` per-IP/global limits.\n\nCloses #7360\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796728977&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7658&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7658&signature=d3ba28bc0e6e7cedfc3bcf86c8356dabae841fe0cee80dd23ef7378834e595c6\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7658?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
